+/*
+ * A folder's Sharing page and Advanced Sharing (Stained Glass OS, net4, i0978)
+ *
+ * Windows' Properties > Sharing (ntshrui) says whether a folder is shared on the
+ * network and at which path, and its Advanced Sharing (an administrator's: the
+ * shield) shares it -- a name, a limit of users, a comment, Everyone's permission
+ * -- or stops sharing it. Here the page asks netapi32 (NetShareEnum); the
+ * buttons start an elevated "rundll32 shell32.dll,SgShareFolder" whose dialog
+ * calls NetShareAdd and NetShareDel, which sg-admind (sg-shell) carries out as a
+ * Samba share. "Share..." shares the folder by its name for the people of this
+ * PC to read, the one-step form of Windows' "Give access to".
